    "updated_at": "2022-11-14T13:21:15Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the heads-up, and apologies for the hassle.\r\nI was aware and since #4588 is already merged a `starship` release for a fix is possible.\r\n\r\nFor posterity let me say that removing the `'static` bound from `pub MyTrait: 'static { type Sub: MyTrait }` isn't a non-breaking change like I thought, but in fact causes some users of this trait to have to amend the `'static` bound to their function declarations if they were requiring `'static` before. Somehow I managed to not notice the mistake despite having fixed these issues in `gitoxide`s own codebase after the change. I hope this lesson learned will help to avoid this and similar mistakes in the future, which unfortunately still hinge on me realizing a change is breaking so [the tooling](https://github.com/Byron/gitoxide/tree/main/cargo-smart-release) can do the right thing hopefully 100% of the time.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
